    <documentation>
Lutron GRAFIK Eye - IR scene control as Control4 lights (light_v2). Requires OS 3.2.0+ to add scene lights.

SETUP
1. Add this driver ONCE. That device is the main "GRAFIK Eye" light.
2. Bind its "IR Sensor" to the IR output with the emitter on the GRAFIK Eye.
3. Actions tab: "Add Scene Light: ..." (or "Add All Scene Lights").
   Each creates a light for that scene in the same room, already set up.
   Nothing to bind on the scene lights. Refresh Composer to see them.

REMOVING A SCENE
Delete that scene light in Composer, then press "Refresh Scene Lights"
on the main device (it also refreshes on its own when the scene changes).

BEHAVIOUR
Main light : On sends "Main On Scene", Off sends OFF. Shows on when any scene is on.
Scene light: On activates its scene. Off sends OFF only if its scene is active.
Only the active scene's light shows on.

The GRAFIK Eye cannot report state over IR, so the driver tracks the last scene
it sent. If someone uses the wall unit directly, use the "Set State Only"
actions to correct it without sending IR.
    </documentation>
